alacritty9 — Alacritty 0.17.0 for 9front. Changelog.
(`pac9 changelog alacritty9` shows this; newest first.)

0.2.1 — 2026-07-26
  Every TUI in an alacritty9 window drew duplicated lines with their tails missing,
  and keystroke-driven apps could not submit input at all. Both are fixed.

    - The child is told the REAL window size. winit's plan9 backend starts at a
      placeholder 1024x768 and learns the truth from the presenter's opening resize
      record — but that was only applied when the event loop DISPATCHED it, after the
      terminal had been sized and the child spawned. A live window handed its child
      COLS=113 LINES=45 while the grid was 88x28: every full-width line wrapped, so
      the app's cursor-up redraws landed a row off. The reader thread now applies a
      resize the moment it reads one.
    - A later resize reaches the child too. /env is not a live channel here (fork
      copies the environment group at exec), so the size is also written to a file
      whose path the child gets in $A9_SIZE_FILE, rewritten on every resize.
    - Raw mode is the UNION of the signals that request it — the alternate screen,
      bracketed paste, and the Kitty keyboard stack (nested pushes counted). Treating
      any single "off" as "leave raw mode" dropped a full-screen app back onto the
      cooked line discipline mid-session, which echoed its keystrokes into the grid
      and swallowed its escape sequences. It also means an app that drives the
      keyboard while rendering INLINE — pi does — gets its keys at all.
    - Damage rects are shaped with the right width: the SizeInfo conversion took
      `columns` from `screen_lines`, so rects were clipped to screen_lines-many
      columns.
    - gl9win2's keyboard proc no longer quits on a transient read error. One failure
      used to end keyboard input for the whole session while the window kept drawing
      and taking mouse input; it now reopens /dev/kbd and retries.

0.2.0 — 2026-07-17
  First versioned release. Rebuilt against a correctness pass on the cc9 C
  runtime the terminal is built on — stubs that used to report success while
  doing nothing (durable fsync, honest file locks, correct O_APPEND, per-thread
  errno, corrected float formatting). No change to the terminal itself: same
  upstream Alacritty 0.17.0, same GL9F frames to the gl9win2 window host,
  render re-verified on bare metal. This just puts alacritty9 on the same
  honest substrate as the rest of the ports. Earlier unversioned installs read
  as '-'; `pac9 upgrade alacritty9` moves them here.
